  * into the same bounce buffer (allocated below 4 GiB). Device blocks are
  * 512 bytes there, which is also the GPT's LBA size on eMMC.
  *
+ * With an "sd-card" property on /sweet-sdhci (mkadt --ginkgo --sd: the microSD
+ * host sdhci@4784000) the card is an SDHC/SDXC one instead: the shim has
+ * already asked the RPM for its supplies (ldoa 5/22), sd_init_card() does the
+ * SD identification (CMD8, ACMD41, RCA from CMD3, 4-bit ACMD6) and the
+ * transfers are the same CMD18/CMD25 (block addressed). The shim moves the
+ * SDCC2 root clock from ABL's 100 MHz (GPLL0) to XO, as in its probe that
+ * identified the card (from 100 MHz the same sequence got CMD55 errors), so
+ * the bus runs at 19.2 MHz (boot-arg sddiv, default 0 = undivided). There is
+ * no cache to flush on an SD card.
+ *
  * Writes are refused unless boot-arg ufsrw=1 is set. Every write is checked
  * against the partition bounds again right before it is issued, so nothing
  * outside the named partition can be written.
